external/terminal-bench/                                              Apache-2.0
    A vendored, modified fork of Terminal-Bench v0.2.18
    (https://github.com/laude-institute/terminal-bench), Copyright the
    Terminal-Bench authors. Full license text: external/terminal-bench/LICENSE.
    Only the 110 upstream task packages referenced by the terminal bank are
    retained; the list is external/terminal-bench/USED_TASKS.txt. HalluWorld's
    runtime-probe modifications inside that tree are marked in their file
    headers and are provided under Apache-2.0 with the surrounding fork.

        Merrill, Shaw, Carlini, et al. Terminal-Bench: A Benchmark for AI
        Agents in Terminal Environments. arXiv:2601.11868

    Task packages may refer to, download, patch, or include further third-party
    components, which keep their own terms. In particular
    original-tasks/make-doom-for-mips/ patches DoomGeneric, which contains work
    Copyright (c) Id Software, Simon Howard, and Raven Software and is GPL-2.0;
    that license text is included beside the task as LICENSE.doomgeneric.

Captured terminal contexts
    Terminal probes embed verbatim tmux pane captures from agent runs inside
    Terminal-Bench task containers, so they contain fragments of those tasks'
    files and command output. HalluWorld's grant covers its questions, golden
    answers, labels, and curation; it does not relicense third-party expression
    appearing inside a captured context.

Dependencies
    MiniGrid and Gymnasium (Apache-2.0) are required by the gridworld and InNav
    tracks. python-chess (GPL-3.0-or-later) is an optional dependency of the
    chess track, installed separately with `pip install halluworld[chess]` and
    not bundled here. Lichess puzzle positions, when enabled, come from the
    Lichess puzzle database (CC0).

Provenance detail, including which terminal tasks were authored by HalluWorld
and which came from upstream: docs/PROVENANCE.md.
